(ns kotoba.kir.alpha-normalization
  "Alpha-normalization of a KIR function: binders renamed by position, so that
  two spellings of the same definition are the same definition.

  ## Why this lives here and not in the callers

  `kotoba.kir.definition-identity/normalize` is a canonical ENCODER over a
  closed tagged value domain. It is not binder-aware: it maps a symbol to
  `[\"sym\" <name>]` verbatim. Measured 2026-09-02, two payloads differing only
  in a binder name hash to different CIDs -- `(+ a 1)` to
  bafyreigucwk5cmuh7b7xwcviysfzuiemmevwqvj6jl3i3wuwvnzdmdmmki and `(+ b 1)` to
  bafyreiazdjhcwy3jj3sigeol5ydpaopblxx3bksbrknxzaoauwxasie6ka. So a caller that
  wants `:alpha-rename-independent` (kotoba-lang `lang/elaboration-pipeline.edn`,
  stage `:definition-cid`) has to rename first.

  Both callers did, separately: `kotoba.codebase.typed-code` and
  `kotoba.compiler.definition-identity` each carried the same five-binder walk
  over the same KIR. kotoba-lang `lang/code-identity.edn` recorded that as a
  residual risk of :ci8 and named the fix -- move the walk INTO kotoba-kir,
  not into a third place. This namespace is that move.

  ## The five binding forms, and what happens to a sixth

  KIR binds a name in exactly five places: a function's `params`, `let`,
  `result-match-of`, `variant-match` and `option-match`. `binding-forms` names
  the four that appear as operators.

  A sixth binding form added to KIR later would not be renamed here.
  `verify-normalized!` refuses a normalized function whose body still contains
  a name this walk DID rename, which is the shape such a form produces when it
  takes a name already bound and lets a reference to it escape. Use
  `normalize-function` unless you have a reason to run the two halves apart --
  it is the pair, and it cannot be forgotten.

  MEASURED LIMIT (2026-09-02). Both copies this namespace replaces documented
  that check as catching any sixth binding form. It does not, and the claim is
  corrected here rather than carried. A form whose binder is a name the walk
  never bound -- `(loop [i 0] (+ i 1))` with no outer `i` -- leaks nothing by
  that test, so `i` is sealed into the identity and two spellings of that
  function get two CIDs. Telling `i` apart from a legitimate free reference to
  a callee needs a table of KIR operators, which kotoba-kir does not own and
  which inventing here would make a second admission gate. So the guard against
  a sixth binding form is `binding-forms` being public, `handles?` answering
  it, and `kotoba.kir-alpha-normalization-test/the-refusal-does-not-catch-a-
  self-contained-unhandled-form` naming the hole -- not a check that closes it.
  A KIR change that adds a binding head must add it to `binding-forms`.

  ## Reconciling the two copies it replaces (measured 2026-09-02)

  The two walks were the same algorithm and differed in two places:

  - `set?`: the compiler's copy renamed inside a set; the codebase's copy had
    no `set?` branch, so a set fell to the leaf and any bound symbol inside it
    survived -- which `verify-normalized!` then refused. The branch is kept.
    It widens a refusal into a CID; it moves no CID that exists, because the
    case it changes is exactly the case that produced no CID before.
  - the leaf: the compiler's copy mapped a host number to the identity's
    admitted `i64`/`f64` form (nbb holds a `.kotoba` integer literal as a
    JavaScript BigInt, which is neither `integer?` nor `number?` in
    ClojureScript); the codebase's copy left the leaf alone, because its own
    encoder admits host floats directly. Neither belongs to alpha-renaming, so
    it is a caller-supplied `:scalar` function, defaulting to `identity`. Each
    caller keeps the leaf it had, byte for byte.

  Nothing else differed, including the counter discipline: ONE left-to-right
  counter over the whole function that never resets, so a canonical name is a
  function of position alone. A counter that restarted per binding form would
  give `k0` to two different binders and make two different functions share an
  identity.

  ## This is not called by `definition-cid`, deliberately

  `kotoba.kir.definition-identity/definition-cid` does NOT normalize
  internally. That is a decision, not an omission:

  1. It hashes a PAYLOAD, whose `:definition/kir` is any KIR value -- a
     `{:op :const}`, a `{:op :do}`, a function. Normalizing internally would
     mean guessing which shape has binders. Seven of the ten frozen vectors in
     kotoba-lang `lang/code-identity-vectors.edn` carry `{:op :const :value 1}`.
  2. Renaming has to happen BEFORE dependency linking, not at hash time. A
     caller replaces callee symbols with `[:kotoba.definition/ref <cid>]` nodes
     after normalizing; a normalizer running at hash time would run after that
     substitution, on a body whose call targets are no longer symbols.
  3. Verification needs the caller's set of call targets to tell a leaked
     binder from a legitimate free name. `definition-cid` does not have it and
     should not: an identity function that asks for a name table is not an
     identity function.
  4. The ten frozen vectors must not move, and an internal step is a step that
     could move them. Measured after this change: all ten are byte-identical.

  The safety this gives up -- that identity cannot be computed over
  un-normalized KIR -- is bought back by `verify-normalized!` refusing at the
  caller, which is also the only place that can check it."
  {:kotoba/export [alpha-normalize binding-forms canonical-binder contract handles? normalize-function symbols-in verify-normalized!]}
  #?(:kotoba (:schemas {:form/r [:record :form/r [[:tag :i64] [:s :string] [:n :i64] [:k :keyword]
                                          [:kids [:list [:ref :form/r]]] [:span :i64] [:data :bytes]]]
                                 :an/state [:record :an/state [[:counter :i64] [:scope [:ref :form/r]] [:bound [:ref :form/r]]]]
                                 :an/res [:record :an/res [[:form [:ref :form/r]] [:state [:ref :an/state]]]]})))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-no-forms [] [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (typed-list-new [:list [:ref :form/r]])))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-one-form [a [:ref :form/r]] [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (typed-list-new [:list [:ref :form/r]] a)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-two-forms [a [:ref :form/r] b [:ref :form/r]] [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (typed-list-new [:list [:ref :form/r]] a b)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-three-forms [a [:ref :form/r] b [:ref :form/r] c [:ref :form/r]] [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (typed-list-new [:list [:ref :form/r]] a b c)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-append-form [xs [:list [:ref :form/r]] x [:ref :form/r]] [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (typed-list-conj [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs x)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-mk [t :i64 s :string n :i64 k :keyword kids [:list [:ref :form/r]]] [:ref :form/r]
     (record-new [:ref :form/r] t s n k kids 0 (bytes-empty))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-nil-form [] [:ref :form/r] (form-mk 0 "" 0 :none (form-no-forms))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-bool-form [b :bool] [:ref :form/r] (form-mk 1 "" (if b 1 0) :none (form-no-forms))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-int-form [n :i64] [:ref :form/r] (form-mk 2 "" n :none (form-no-forms))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-string-form [s :string] [:ref :form/r] (form-mk 3 s 0 :none (form-no-forms))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-keyword-form [k :keyword] [:ref :form/r] (form-mk 4 "" 0 k (form-no-forms))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-symbol-form [s :string] [:ref :form/r] (form-mk 5 s 0 :none (form-no-forms))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-form-seq [kids [:list [:ref :form/r]]] [:ref :form/r] (form-mk 6 "" 0 :none kids)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-form-vec [kids [:list [:ref :form/r]]] [:ref :form/r] (form-mk 7 "" 0 :none kids)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-form-set [kids [:list [:ref :form/r]]] [:ref :form/r] (form-mk 8 "" 0 :none kids)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-form-map [kids [:list [:ref :form/r]]] [:ref :form/r] (form-mk 9 "" 0 :none kids)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-tag-of [f [:ref :form/r]] :i64 (record-get [:ref :form/r] f :tag)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-kids-of [f [:ref :form/r]] [:list [:ref :form/r]] (record-get [:ref :form/r] f :kids)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-int-value [f [:ref :form/r]] :i64 (record-get [:ref :form/r] f :n)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-string-value [f [:ref :form/r]] :string (record-get [:ref :form/r] f :s)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-symbol-value [f [:ref :form/r]] :string (record-get [:ref :form/r] f :s)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-keyword-value [f [:ref :form/r]] :keyword (record-get [:ref :form/r] f :k)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-bool-value [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool (= 1 (record-get [:ref :form/r] f :n))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-is-nil? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool (= 0 (form-tag-of f))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-is-bool? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool (= 1 (form-tag-of f))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-is-int? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool (= 2 (form-tag-of f))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-is-string? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool (= 3 (form-tag-of f))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-is-keyword? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool (= 4 (form-tag-of f))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-is-symbol? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool (= 5 (form-tag-of f))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-is-seq? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool (= 6 (form-tag-of f))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-is-vec? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool (= 7 (form-tag-of f))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-is-set? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool (= 8 (form-tag-of f))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-is-map? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool (= 9 (form-tag-of f))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-is-list-like? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool (or (= 6 (form-tag-of f)) (= 7 (form-tag-of f)))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-is-true? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool (and (= 1 (form-tag-of f)) (= 1 (record-get [:ref :form/r] f :n)))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-count-of [f [:ref :form/r]] :i64 (vector-count (form-kids-of f))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-nth-of [f [:ref :form/r] i :i64] [:ref :form/r]
     (if (and (>= i 0) (< i (form-count-of f)))
       (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] (form-kids-of f) i)
       (form-nil-form))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-first-of [f [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r] (form-nth-of f 0)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-lookup-from [kids [:list [:ref :form/r]] key [:ref :form/r] i :i64] [:ref :form/r]
     (let [n (vector-count kids)]
       (loop [j i]
         (if (>= (+ j 1) n)
           (form-nil-form)
           (if (form-eq (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] kids j) key)
             (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] kids (+ j 1))
             (recur (+ j 2))))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-form-get [m [:ref :form/r] key [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (form-lookup-from (form-kids-of m) key 0)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-lookup-has [kids [:list [:ref :form/r]] key [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (let [n (vector-count kids)]
       (loop [j 0]
         (if (>= (+ j 1) n)
           false
           (if (form-eq (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] kids j) key)
             true
             (recur (+ j 2))))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-form-has? [m [:ref :form/r] key [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (form-lookup-has (form-kids-of m) key)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-member? [xs [:list [:ref :form/r]] x [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (let [n (vector-count xs)]
       (loop [i 0]
         (if (>= i n) false
           (if (form-eq (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs i) x) true (recur (inc i))))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-ordered-eq [xs [:list [:ref :form/r]] ys [:list [:ref :form/r]]] :bool
     (let [n (vector-count xs)]
       (if (= n (vector-count ys))
         (loop [i 0]
           (if (>= i n) true
             (if (form-eq (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs i) (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] ys i))
               (recur (inc i))
               false)))
         false))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-set-eq [xs [:list [:ref :form/r]] ys [:list [:ref :form/r]]] :bool
     (let [n (vector-count xs)]
       (if (= n (vector-count ys))
         (loop [i 0]
           (if (>= i n) true
             (if (form-member? ys (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs i)) (recur (inc i)) false)))
         false))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-map-eq [xs [:list [:ref :form/r]] ys [:list [:ref :form/r]]] :bool
     (let [n (vector-count xs)]
       (if (= n (vector-count ys))
         (loop [j 0]
           (if (>= (+ j 1) n) true
             (let [k (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs j)]
               (if (and (form-lookup-has ys k)
                        (form-eq (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs (+ j 1)) (form-lookup-from ys k 0)))
                 (recur (+ j 2))
                 false))))
         false))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-eq
     "Structural equality, as `=` on the host's data: a list and a vector are
     different kinds here (as are they to the reader), sets and maps compare
     without order."
     [a [:ref :form/r] b [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (let [t (form-tag-of a)]
       (and (= t (form-tag-of b))
            (cond
              (= t 0) true
              (= t 1) (= (record-get [:ref :form/r] a :n) (record-get [:ref :form/r] b :n))
              (= t 2) (= (record-get [:ref :form/r] a :n) (record-get [:ref :form/r] b :n))
              (= t 3) (string=? (record-get [:ref :form/r] a :s) (record-get [:ref :form/r] b :s))
              (= t 4) (= (record-get [:ref :form/r] a :k) (record-get [:ref :form/r] b :k))
              (= t 5) (string=? (record-get [:ref :form/r] a :s) (record-get [:ref :form/r] b :s))
              (= t 8) (form-set-eq (form-kids-of a) (form-kids-of b))
              (= t 9) (form-map-eq (form-kids-of a) (form-kids-of b))
              :else (form-ordered-eq (form-kids-of a) (form-kids-of b)))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-rest-list
     "The kids of F after the first, as a list."
     [f [:ref :form/r]] [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (let [xs (form-kids-of f)
           n (vector-count xs)]
       (loop [i 1 acc (form-no-forms)]
         (if (>= i n)
           acc
           (recur (inc i) (typed-list-conj [:list [:ref :form/r]] acc (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs i))))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-last-of [f [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (form-nth-of f (dec (form-count-of f)))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-cons-onto [x [:ref :form/r] xs [:list [:ref :form/r]]] [:list [:ref :form/r]]
     (let [n (vector-count xs)]
       (loop [i 0 acc (form-one-form x)]
         (if (>= i n)
           acc
           (recur (inc i) (typed-list-conj [:list [:ref :form/r]] acc (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs i))))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-assoc-form
     "Map M with K bound to V: the first entry whose key is K keeps its place and
     takes V, else K V are appended (as `assoc` on the host's map)."
     [m [:ref :form/r] k [:ref :form/r] v [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (let [xs (form-kids-of m)
           n (vector-count xs)]
       (if (form-lookup-has xs k)
         (form-form-map
          (loop [j 0 acc (form-no-forms)]
            (if (>= (+ j 1) n)
              acc
              (let [key (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs j)]
                (recur (+ j 2)
                       (typed-list-conj [:list [:ref :form/r]]
                                        (typed-list-conj [:list [:ref :form/r]] acc key)
                                        (if (form-eq key k) v (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs (+ j 1)))))))))
         (form-form-map (typed-list-conj [:list [:ref :form/r]] (typed-list-conj [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs k) v))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-call0 [name :string] [:ref :form/r] (form-form-seq (form-one-form (form-symbol-form name)))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-call1 [name :string a [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (form-form-seq (form-two-forms (form-symbol-form name) a))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-call2 [name :string a [:ref :form/r] b [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (form-form-seq (form-three-forms (form-symbol-form name) a b))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-call3 [name :string a [:ref :form/r] b [:ref :form/r] c [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (form-form-seq (typed-list-conj [:list [:ref :form/r]] (form-three-forms (form-symbol-form name) a b) c))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-call4 [name :string a [:ref :form/r] b [:ref :form/r] c [:ref :form/r] d [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (form-form-seq (typed-list-conj [:list [:ref :form/r]] (typed-list-conj [:list [:ref :form/r]] (form-three-forms (form-symbol-form name) a b) c) d))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-call5 [name :string a [:ref :form/r] b [:ref :form/r] c [:ref :form/r] d [:ref :form/r] e [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (form-form-seq (typed-list-conj [:list [:ref :form/r]] (typed-list-conj [:list [:ref :form/r]] (typed-list-conj [:list [:ref :form/r]] (form-three-forms (form-symbol-form name) a b) c) d) e))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-call6 [name :string a [:ref :form/r] b [:ref :form/r] c [:ref :form/r] d [:ref :form/r] e [:ref :form/r] f [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (form-form-seq (typed-list-conj [:list [:ref :form/r]] (typed-list-conj [:list [:ref :form/r]] (typed-list-conj [:list [:ref :form/r]] (typed-list-conj [:list [:ref :form/r]] (form-three-forms (form-symbol-form name) a b) c) d) e) f))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-vec2 [a [:ref :form/r] b [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r] (form-form-vec (form-two-forms a b))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-vec3 [a [:ref :form/r] b [:ref :form/r] c [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r] (form-form-vec (form-three-forms a b c))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-vec4 [a [:ref :form/r] b [:ref :form/r] c [:ref :form/r] d [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (form-form-vec (typed-list-conj [:list [:ref :form/r]] (form-three-forms a b c) d))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-vec5 [a [:ref :form/r] b [:ref :form/r] c [:ref :form/r] d [:ref :form/r] e [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (form-form-vec (typed-list-conj [:list [:ref :form/r]] (typed-list-conj [:list [:ref :form/r]] (form-three-forms a b c) d) e))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- form-vec6 [a [:ref :form/r] b [:ref :form/r] c [:ref :form/r] d [:ref :form/r] e [:ref :form/r] f [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (form-form-vec (typed-list-conj [:list [:ref :form/r]] (typed-list-conj [:list [:ref :form/r]] (typed-list-conj [:list [:ref :form/r]] (form-three-forms a b c) d) e) f))))



#?(:kotoba
   (defn contract [] :keyword :kotoba.kir.alpha-normalization/v1)
   :default
   (def contract
     "The versioned shape of what `alpha-normalize` returns. Bumped when that map
     changes, so a consumer keying on it is never handed a different answer under
     the same name."
     :kotoba.kir.alpha-normalization/v1))



#?(:kotoba
   (defn binding-forms
     "The KIR operators that bind a name in their body."
     [] [:set :symbol]
     (typed-set-new [:set :symbol] (symbol "let") (symbol "result-match-of") (symbol "variant-match") (symbol "option-match")))
   :default
   (def binding-forms
     "The KIR operators that bind a name in their body.

     A function's `params` is the fifth binding site and is not an operator, so
     it is not here; `alpha-normalize` binds it before walking. This set is the
     checkable form of the five-binder claim: `handles?` answers it, and
     `verify-normalized!` catches the case where the answer became wrong."
     '#{let result-match-of variant-match option-match}))



#?(:kotoba
   (defn- sym-is? [f [:ref :form/r] name :string] :bool
     (and (form-is-symbol? f) (string=? (form-symbol-value f) name)))
   :default
   (defn handles?
     "True when OP is a KIR binding operator this walk renames.

     False for everything else, including a binding form KIR gains later. False
     is not the same as safe: it means the walk treats OP as an ordinary call,
     and `verify-normalized!` is what turns that into a refusal."
     [op]
     (contains? binding-forms op)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn handles?
     "True when OP is a KIR binding operator this walk renames."
     [op [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (or (sym-is? op "let") (sym-is? op "result-match-of") (sym-is? op "variant-match") (sym-is? op "option-match"))))



(def ^:private binder-prefix "k")



#?(:kotoba
   (defn canonical-binder
     "The canonical name for the Nth binder in a function, counting left to right
     across the whole body."
     [n :i64] :symbol
     (symbol (string-concat binder-prefix (string-from-i64 n))))
   :default
   (defn canonical-binder
     "The canonical name for the Nth binder in a function, counting left to right
     across the whole body. Public because the two callers' fixtures name `k0`,
     `k1` and would otherwise be asserting a spelling nothing declares."
     [n]
     (symbol (str binder-prefix n))))



#?(:kotoba
   (defn- ref-type-vector? [f [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (and (form-is-vec? f) (form-eq (form-first-of f) (form-keyword-form :ref)) (= 2 (form-count-of f))))
   :default
   (defn- ref-type-vector?
     "`[:ref schema-name]` names a schema, not a local. Renaming inside it would
     rewrite a type."
     [form]
     (and (vector? form) (= :ref (first form)) (= 2 (count form)))))



#?(:kotoba
   (defn- st [counter :i64 scope [:ref :form/r] bound [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :an/state]
     (record-new [:ref :an/state] counter scope bound))
   :default
   (declare normalize-form))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- st-counter [s [:ref :an/state]] :i64 (record-get [:ref :an/state] s :counter)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- st-scope [s [:ref :an/state]] [:ref :form/r] (record-get [:ref :an/state] s :scope)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- st-bound [s [:ref :an/state]] [:ref :form/r] (record-get [:ref :an/state] s :bound)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- res [f [:ref :form/r] s [:ref :an/state]] [:ref :an/res] (record-new [:ref :an/res] f s)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- res-form [r [:ref :an/res]] [:ref :form/r] (record-get [:ref :an/res] r :form)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- res-state [r [:ref :an/res]] [:ref :an/state] (record-get [:ref :an/res] r :state)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- fget [m [:ref :form/r] k :keyword] [:ref :form/r] (form-form-get m (form-keyword-form k))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- member-of? [xs [:list [:ref :form/r]] x [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (let [n (vector-count xs)]
       (loop [i 0]
         (if (>= i n) false (if (form-eq (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs i) x) true (recur (inc i))))))))

#?(:kotoba
   ;; A set with X added (once).
   (defn- set-add [s [:ref :form/r] x [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (if (member-of? (form-kids-of s) x) s (form-form-set (form-append-form (form-kids-of s) x)))))

#?(:kotoba
   ;; (get scope f f)
   (defn- scoped [scope [:ref :form/r] f [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (if (form-form-has? scope f) (form-form-get scope f) f)))



#?(:kotoba
   (defn- normalize-seq [forms [:list [:ref :form/r]] state [:ref :an/state]] [:ref :an/res]
     (let [n (vector-count forms)]
       (loop [i 0 out (form-no-forms) s state]
         (if (>= i n)
           (res (form-form-vec out) s)
           (let [r (normalize-form (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] forms i) s)]
             (recur (inc i) (form-append-form out (res-form r)) (res-state r)))))))
   :default
   (defn- normalize-seq [forms state]
     (reduce (fn [{:keys [out state]} form]
               (let [{:keys [form state]} (normalize-form form state)]
                 {:out (conj out form) :state state}))
             {:out [] :state state}
             forms)))



#?(:kotoba
   (defn- bind-one [state [:ref :an/state] nm [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :an/res]
     (let [renamed (form-symbol-form (string-concat binder-prefix (string-from-i64 (st-counter state))))]
       (res renamed (st (inc (st-counter state))
                        (form-assoc-form (st-scope state) nm renamed)
                        (set-add (st-bound state) nm)))))
   :default
   (defn- bind-one [state nm]
     (let [renamed (canonical-binder (:counter state))]
       {:renamed renamed
        :state (-> state
                   (update :counter inc)
                   (update :scope assoc nm renamed)
                   (update :bound conj nm))})))



#?(:kotoba
   (defn- restore-scope [r [:ref :an/res] outer [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :an/res]
     (let [s (res-state r)]
       (res (res-form r) (st (st-counter s) outer (st-bound s)))))
   :default
   (defn- with-scope
     "Run F with STATE's scope, then restore the outer scope but keep the counter
     and the record of which names were bound.

     Restoring the scope is what makes a binder's reach its own body; keeping the
     counter is what makes the canonical name a function of position rather than
     of nesting depth."
     [state f]
     (let [outer (:scope state)
           {:keys [form state]} (f state)]
       {:form form :state (assoc state :scope outer)})))



#?(:kotoba
   (defn- normalize-let [argf [:ref :form/r] state [:ref :an/state]] [:ref :an/res]
     (let [bindings (form-nth-of argf 0)
           n (form-count-of bindings)]
       (loop [i 0 pairs (form-no-forms) s state]
         (if (>= (+ i 1) n)
           (let [b (normalize-form (form-nth-of argf 1) s)]
             (restore-scope
              (res (form-call2 "let" (form-form-vec pairs) (res-form b)) (res-state b))
              (st-scope state)))
           (let [v (normalize-form (form-nth-of bindings (+ i 1)) s)
                 b (bind-one (res-state v) (form-nth-of bindings i))]
             (recur (+ i 2)
                    (form-append-form (form-append-form pairs (res-form b)) (res-form v))
                    (res-state b)))))))
   :default
   (defn- normalize-form
     "Rename binders to canonical names, leaving everything else alone."
     [form state]
     (cond
       (symbol? form)
       {:form (get (:scope state) form form) :state state}

       (ref-type-vector? form)
       {:form form :state state}

       (map? form)
       (let [{:keys [out state]} (normalize-seq (mapcat identity form) state)]
         {:form (apply hash-map out) :state state})

       (vector? form)
       (let [{:keys [out state]} (normalize-seq form state)]
         {:form out :state state})

       (set? form)
       (let [{:keys [out state]} (normalize-seq (seq form) state)]
         {:form (set out) :state state})

       (seq? form)
       (let [[op & args] form]
         (case op
           let
           (with-scope
             state
             (fn [state]
               (let [[bindings body] args
                     {:keys [pairs state]}
                     (reduce (fn [{:keys [pairs state]} [nm value]]
                               ;; The value is normalized in the OUTER scope and
                               ;; the binder introduced after, so `(let [x x] x)`
                               ;; keeps its two `x`es distinct.
                               (let [{value :form state :state} (normalize-form value state)
                                     {:keys [renamed state]} (bind-one state nm)]
                                 {:pairs (conj pairs renamed value) :state state}))
                             {:pairs [] :state state}
                             (partition 2 bindings))
                     {body :form state :state} (normalize-form body state)]
                 {:form (list 'let pairs body) :state state})))

           result-match-of
           (let [[type result-form ok-name ok-body err-name err-body] args
                 {result-form :form state :state} (normalize-form result-form state)
                 {ok :form state :state}
                 (with-scope state
                   (fn [state]
                     (let [{:keys [renamed state]} (bind-one state ok-name)
                           {body :form state :state} (normalize-form ok-body state)]
                       {:form [renamed body] :state state})))
                 {err :form state :state}
                 (with-scope state
                   (fn [state]
                     (let [{:keys [renamed state]} (bind-one state err-name)
                           {body :form state :state} (normalize-form err-body state)]
                       {:form [renamed body] :state state})))]
             {:form (list 'result-match-of type result-form
                          (first ok) (second ok) (first err) (second err))
              :state state})

           variant-match
           (let [[type value-form branches] args
                 {value-form :form state :state} (normalize-form value-form state)
                 {:keys [out state]}
                 (reduce (fn [{:keys [out state]} [tag binder body]]
                           (let [{branch :form state :state}
                                 (with-scope state
                                   (fn [state]
                                     (let [{:keys [renamed state]} (bind-one state binder)
                                           {body :form state :state} (normalize-form body state)]
                                       {:form [tag renamed body] :state state})))]
                             {:out (conj out branch) :state state}))
                         {:out [] :state state}
                         branches)]
             {:form (list 'variant-match type value-form out) :state state})

           option-match
           (let [[type option-form none-body some-name some-body] args
                 {option-form :form state :state} (normalize-form option-form state)
                 {none-body :form state :state} (normalize-form none-body state)
                 {some-part :form state :state}
                 (with-scope state
                   (fn [state]
                     (let [{:keys [renamed state]} (bind-one state some-name)
                           {body :form state :state} (normalize-form some-body state)]
                       {:form [renamed body] :state state})))]
             {:form (list 'option-match type option-form none-body
                          (first some-part) (second some-part))
              :state state})

           ;; Any other operator: the operator symbol itself may be a call target
           ;; and is renamed only if it is locally bound, which it never is.
           (let [{:keys [out state]} (normalize-seq args state)]
             {:form (cons (get (:scope state) op op) out) :state state})))

       :else {:form ((:scalar state) form) :state state})))

#?(:kotoba
   ;; Bind NAME, normalize BODY under it, restore the scope: the pair [renamed body].
   (defn- scoped-branch [name [:ref :form/r] body [:ref :form/r] state [:ref :an/state]] [:ref :an/res]
     (let [b (bind-one state name)
           r (normalize-form body (res-state b))]
       (restore-scope (res (form-vec2 (res-form b) (res-form r)) (res-state r)) (st-scope state)))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- normalize-result-match [argf [:ref :form/r] state [:ref :an/state]] [:ref :an/res]
     (let [rf (normalize-form (form-nth-of argf 1) state)
           ok (scoped-branch (form-nth-of argf 2) (form-nth-of argf 3) (res-state rf))
           er (scoped-branch (form-nth-of argf 4) (form-nth-of argf 5) (res-state ok))]
       (res (form-call6 "result-match-of" (form-nth-of argf 0) (res-form rf)
                        (form-nth-of (res-form ok) 0) (form-nth-of (res-form ok) 1)
                        (form-nth-of (res-form er) 0) (form-nth-of (res-form er) 1))
            (res-state er)))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- normalize-variant-match [argf [:ref :form/r] state [:ref :an/state]] [:ref :an/res]
     (let [vf (normalize-form (form-nth-of argf 1) state)
           branches (form-nth-of argf 2)
           n (form-count-of branches)]
       (loop [i 0 out (form-no-forms) s (res-state vf)]
         (if (>= i n)
           (res (form-call3 "variant-match" (form-nth-of argf 0) (res-form vf) (form-form-vec out)) s)
           (let [br (form-nth-of branches i)
                 r (scoped-branch (form-nth-of br 1) (form-nth-of br 2) s)]
             (recur (inc i)
                    (form-append-form out (form-vec3 (form-nth-of br 0) (form-nth-of (res-form r) 0) (form-nth-of (res-form r) 1)))
                    (res-state r))))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- normalize-option-match [argf [:ref :form/r] state [:ref :an/state]] [:ref :an/res]
     (let [of (normalize-form (form-nth-of argf 1) state)
           nb (normalize-form (form-nth-of argf 2) (res-state of))
           sp (scoped-branch (form-nth-of argf 3) (form-nth-of argf 4) (res-state nb))]
       (res (form-call5 "option-match" (form-nth-of argf 0) (res-form of) (res-form nb)
                        (form-nth-of (res-form sp) 0) (form-nth-of (res-form sp) 1))
            (res-state sp)))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- rebuild-map [flat [:list [:ref :form/r]]] [:ref :form/r]
     (let [n (vector-count flat)]
       (loop [j 0 m (form-form-map (form-no-forms))]
         (if (>= (+ j 1) n)
           m
           (recur (+ j 2) (form-assoc-form m (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] flat j) (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] flat (+ j 1)))))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- rebuild-set [items [:list [:ref :form/r]]] [:ref :form/r]
     (let [n (vector-count items)]
       (loop [i 0 s (form-form-set (form-no-forms))]
         (if (>= i n)
           s
           (recur (inc i) (set-add s (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] items i))))))))

#?(:kotoba
   ;; Rename binders to canonical names, leaving everything else alone.
   (defn- normalize-form [f [:ref :form/r] state [:ref :an/state]] [:ref :an/res]
     (cond
       (form-is-symbol? f) (res (scoped (st-scope state) f) state)
       (ref-type-vector? f) (res f state)
       (form-is-map? f)
       (let [r (normalize-seq (form-kids-of f) state)]
         (res (rebuild-map (form-kids-of (res-form r))) (res-state r)))
       (form-is-vec? f) (normalize-seq (form-kids-of f) state)
       (form-is-set? f)
       (let [r (normalize-seq (form-kids-of f) state)]
         (res (rebuild-set (form-kids-of (res-form r))) (res-state r)))
       (form-is-seq? f)
       (let [op (form-first-of f)
             args (form-rest-list f)
             argf (form-form-seq args)]
         (cond
           (sym-is? op "let") (normalize-let argf state)
           (sym-is? op "result-match-of") (normalize-result-match argf state)
           (sym-is? op "variant-match") (normalize-variant-match argf state)
           (sym-is? op "option-match") (normalize-option-match argf state)
           :else
           (let [r (normalize-seq args state)]
             (res (form-form-seq (form-cons-onto (scoped (st-scope (res-state r)) op) (form-kids-of (res-form r))))
                  (res-state r)))))
       :else (res f state))))



#?(:kotoba
   (defn- symbols-into [f [:ref :form/r] acc [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (cond
       (form-is-symbol? f) (set-add acc f)
       (or (form-is-seq? f) (form-is-vec? f) (form-is-set? f) (form-is-map? f))
       (let [xs (form-kids-of f)
             n (vector-count xs)]
         (loop [i 0 a acc]
           (if (>= i n) a (recur (inc i) (symbols-into (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] xs i) a)))))
       :else acc))
   :default
   (defn symbols-in
     "Every symbol reachable in FORM. Public because `verify-normalized!` is the
     checkable half of the five-binder claim and a caller may want to state it
     about something other than a whole function."
     [form]
     (into #{} (filter symbol?) (tree-seq coll? seq form))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn symbols-in
     "Every symbol reachable in FORM."
     [f [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (symbols-into f (form-form-set (form-no-forms)))))



#?(:kotoba
   (defn- bind-params [params [:ref :form/r] state [:ref :an/state]] [:ref :an/state]
     (let [n (form-count-of params)]
       (loop [i 0 s state]
         (if (>= i n) s (recur (inc i) (res-state (bind-one s (form-nth-of params i))))))))
   :default
   (defn alpha-normalize
     "Canonically rename one KIR function's binders.

     FUNCTION is `{:params [sym ...] :body <kir>}`. Returns
     `{:params :body :bound}`, where `:bound` is the set of ORIGINAL names this
     walk renamed -- `verify-normalized!` needs it, and it is otherwise the only
     record of what the walk claimed to have handled.

     OPTS may carry `:scalar`, a function applied to every leaf that is not a
     symbol, collection or `[:ref _]`. It defaults to `identity`. It exists
     because the compiler must map a host number to the identity's admitted
     `i64`/`f64` form -- under nbb a `.kotoba` integer literal is a JavaScript
     BigInt, which is neither `integer?` nor `number?` -- while the codebase's own
     encoder admits host floats directly. That is a canonicalization of values,
     not of binders, so it is the caller's and not this walk's.

     Does NOT verify. Call `verify-normalized!`, or use `normalize-function`."
     ([function] (alpha-normalize function nil))
     ([{:keys [params body]} {:keys [scalar]}]
      (let [state (reduce (fn [state nm] (:state (bind-one state nm)))
                          {:counter 0 :scope {} :bound #{} :scalar (or scalar identity)}
                          params)
            renamed-params (mapv #(get (:scope state) %) params)
            {body :form state :state} (normalize-form body state)]
        {:params renamed-params :body body :bound (:bound state)}))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- renamed-params [params [:ref :form/r] scope [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (let [n (form-count-of params)]
       (loop [i 0 out (form-no-forms)]
         (if (>= i n)
           (form-form-vec out)
           (recur (inc i) (form-append-form out (form-form-get scope (form-nth-of params i)))))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn alpha-normalize
     "Canonically rename one KIR function's binders. FUNCTION is a map with
     :params and :body; answers a map with :params :body :bound."
     [function [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
     (let [params (fget function :params)
           state (bind-params params (st 0 (form-form-map (form-no-forms)) (form-form-set (form-no-forms))))
           rp (renamed-params params (st-scope state))
           r (normalize-form (fget function :body) state)
           m0 (form-form-map (form-no-forms))
           m1 (form-assoc-form m0 (form-keyword-form :params) rp)
           m2 (form-assoc-form m1 (form-keyword-form :body) (res-form r))]
       (form-assoc-form m2 (form-keyword-form :bound) (st-bound (res-state r))))))



#?(:kotoba
   (defn- leaks? [bound [:list [:ref :form/r]] present [:ref :form/r] targets [:ref :form/r]] :bool
     (let [n (vector-count bound)]
       (loop [i 0]
         (if (>= i n)
           false
           (let [b (typed-list-nth [:list [:ref :form/r]] bound i)]
             (if (and (member-of? (form-kids-of present) b)
                      (not (member-of? (form-kids-of targets) b)))
               true
               (recur (inc i))))))))
   :default
   (defn verify-normalized!
     "Refuse a normalized function whose body still contains a source-chosen
     binder name. Returns NORMALIZED when it is clean, so it composes.

     This is what makes `binding-forms` checkable instead of assumed: a binding
     form KIR gains later leaves its binder in the body, and this throws rather
     than letting it be hashed. A name in CALL-TARGETS is a legitimate free
     reference to another definition, not a leak.

     OPTS may carry `:problem`, the keyword recorded on the thrown `ex-info`.
     It defaults to `:kotoba.kir.alpha-normalization/binder-not-normalized`. The
     two callers pass their own, because a refusal reason is part of each
     caller's diagnostic vocabulary and renaming theirs would change what a
     consumer of their errors matches on."
     ([normalized call-targets] (verify-normalized! normalized call-targets nil))
     ([{:keys [body bound] :as normalized} call-targets {:keys [problem]}]
      (let [present (symbols-in body)
            leaked (remove #(contains? call-targets %) (filter present bound))
            problem (or problem ::binder-not-normalized)]
        (when (seq leaked)
          (throw (ex-info (name problem)
                          {:problem problem
                           :symbols (vec (sort (map str leaked)))
                           :hint "a KIR binding form is not handled by alpha-normalize"})))
        normalized))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn verify-normalized!
     "Refuse a normalized function whose body still contains a source-chosen
     binder name; answers NORMALIZED when clean. The Kotoba twin aborts with the
     problem keyword and the hint (the host's data also lists the symbols)."
     ([normalized [:ref :form/r] call-targets [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
      (verify-normalized! normalized call-targets :kotoba.kir.alpha-normalization/binder-not-normalized))
     ([normalized [:ref :form/r] call-targets [:ref :form/r] problem :keyword] [:ref :form/r]
      (if (leaks? (form-kids-of (fget normalized :bound)) (symbols-in (fget normalized :body)) call-targets)
        (throw (ex-info "binder not normalized"
                        {:problem problem :hint "a KIR binding form is not handled by alpha-normalize"}))
        normalized))))



#?(:kotoba
   (defn normalize-function
     "`alpha-normalize` then `verify-normalized!`: the pair, so neither half can
     be forgotten."
     ([function [:ref :form/r] call-targets [:ref :form/r]] [:ref :form/r]
      (verify-normalized! (alpha-normalize function) call-targets))
     ([function [:ref :form/r] call-targets [:ref :form/r] problem :keyword] [:ref :form/r]
      (verify-normalized! (alpha-normalize function) call-targets problem)))
   :default
   (defn normalize-function
     "`alpha-normalize` then `verify-normalized!`: the pair, so neither half can
     be forgotten. Returns `{:params :body :bound}`.

     OPTS takes both `:scalar` and `:problem`."
     ([function call-targets] (normalize-function function call-targets nil))
     ([function call-targets opts]
      (verify-normalized! (alpha-normalize function opts) call-targets opts))))
